## Cache Requirement / Optionality Logic

The decision of whether cache is **required** (Redis must be available) or **optional** (in-memory fallback is acceptable) is controlled entirely by **`CacheFactory.shouldUseMemoryStore()`** in `/src/lib/cache/cache-factory.ts`:

| Environment | `CACHE_HOST` env var set | Store used | Redis required? |
|-------------|--------------------------|------------|-----------------|
| `test` | irrelevant | `MemoryCacheStore` | **No** -- always uses memory in tests |
| `development` | **No** (unset/empty) | `MemoryCacheStore` | **No** -- falls back to memory if no Redis configured |
| `development` | **Yes** (e.g. `localhost`) | `RedisCacheStore` | **Yes** -- attempts Redis connection |
| `production` (or any other) | irrelevant | `RedisCacheStore` | **Yes** -- always requires Redis |

**Key takeaway:** In `test` and in `development` without `CACHE_HOST` set, the cache layer is purely in-memory and Redis is **not required**. In `production` and in `development` with `CACHE_HOST` set, Redis **is required** -- the app will attempt to connect and will log warnings on errors but will not crash (errors are caught and logged, not thrown).

